 ### [Coordinate Space Conversion](1785-coordinate-space-conversion.md)
-Coordinate Space Conversion defines the deterministic arithmetic for mapping between continuous world coordinates, continuous voxel coordinates, discrete integer voxel indices, and block indices in a sparse voxel grid [1785-coordinate-space-conversion.md]. It solves the problem of accurately locating which voxel contains a given point and converting that voxel back to world space, ensuring consistency across host (CPU), device (GPU), and shader (GLSL) execution paths. It differs from [Voxel Grid Initialization](2168-voxel-grid-initialization.md) by performing the per-point arithmetic rather than static bounding box setup, and from [World to UVW Normalization](2229-world-to-uvw-normalization.md) by operating in physical units and integer indices rather than normalized $[0, 1]$ texture coordinates.
