 ### [Voxel Grid Initialization](2168-voxel-grid-initialization.md)
-Voxel Grid Initialization establishes the foundational data structures and memory layouts required for volume rendering, specifically configuring scene boundaries, grid resolutions, and active voxel states [2168-voxel-grid-initialization.md]. It solves the problem of transitioning from abstract scene parameters (bounding boxes, camera frustums) to a concrete, addressable 3D grid representation. It differs from [Coordinate Space Conversion](1785-coordinate-space-conversion.md) by focusing on memory allocation and state activation rather than coordinate transformation, and from [Sparse Voxel Storage and Chunking](15595-sparse-voxel-storage-and-chunking.md) by often dealing with the initial population of dense or semi-dense grids before sparsification or chunking strategies are applied.
