 ### [Index Computation and Mapping](15596-index-computation-and-mapping.md)
-Index Computation and Mapping defines the algorithms for translating continuous 3D spatial coordinates into discrete linear indices within a voxel grid data structure [15596-index-computation-and-mapping.md]. It solves the problem of spatial localization, enabling efficient ray marching, point cloud queries, and isosurface extraction by mapping world positions to specific memory locations [G]. This family distinguishes itself from [Spatial Hashing](5002-spatial-hashing.md) by guaranteeing deterministic, collision-free indexing for all points within the grid bounds, and from [Sparse Voxel Storage and Chunking](15595-sparse-voxel-storage-and-chunking.md) by relying on fixed memory layouts rather than dynamic allocation [G].
